From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homescoop <homescoop@ai-ecoverse.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:35:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasi: build uv for wasm32-wasip1-threads

Workspace and crate manifests for slicc's kernel (WASI preview1 with
WASIX threads, sockets and processes):
- [patch.crates-io] for eight crates homescoop patches (homescoop-crates/,
  unpacked and patched by apply.sh): hyper-util dials over wasix-net;
  cargo-util and rustls-native-certs compile on WASI; reqsign and
  astral-reqwest treat wasm32-unknown, not every wasm32, as the browser.
- wasix-command (homescoop's crate, feature tokio) for std::process and
  tokio::process, which WASI does not have.
- indicatif's wasmbind (std::time on WASI); ctrlc and diskus only off
  WASI (no signals; no unix metadata, so cache size adds file lengths).
- uv-extract reads at an offset with std::os::wasi::fs::FileExt.
- The uv binary's recursion limit: run()'s future is deeper on wasm32.
